Avoid clichés: stock names and concepts of any genre (like "Dark Lord", "Ancient Forest", "Dragon Mountain", "The Chosen One", "Station Alpha") are forbidden; honour the genre and tone the world seed chose, whether myth, fantasy, science fiction, history or something else. Everything must have a distinctive, concrete logic of its own; that logic must belong to this entity and to this corner of the world, and must not lean on images repeated everywhere in the world (the list of tired images). Names must fit the world's naming language.
